<task id="146" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C10 part 2 (server) — every BFF writer of a child record assigns its owner: the named Secure owner team when the parent is secure, the parent's BU default team otherwise; refuse when unresolved; ArchTest census of owner-less creates (#1034)</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; defect C10 half 2; GitHub #1034 / ISS-007)</phase>
    <gate>after 144 (named team + resolver secure branch) and 145 (owner-role child privileges) merge; AND after word-add-in-r1 PR #1045 is merged to master and master is merged into this branch (it wires the Office writers and rewrites RecordOwnershipResolver.cs). SHIP-TOGETHER: must not be deployed to a shared environment before task 149 merges (see constraints).</gate>
    <status>completed-with-escalation</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-boundary .cs change across ~20 BFF writers (tags bff-api, auth, security); modifies ownership of user-facing records; new ArchTest.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting security change touching ~20 writers in five modules (ExternalAccess, Communication, AI, Finance, Compose) with per-writer failure contracts; a missed writer is a silent disclosure of a secure record's child.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies RecordOwnershipResolver.cs (also edited by 144 and PR #1045), ExternalDataService.cs and ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs (ExternalAccess exclusive zone — also edited by amended task 056 for the matter/WA event routes: serialize with 056), CommunicationService.cs and the AI analysis writers; tasks 147/148/149 build on the owner hook this task installs. File overlap with task 152 (notifications — also edits ExternalDataService.cs, EventEndpoints.cs, TaskActionCore.cs and TodoGenerationService.cs to set Assigned To): serialize with 152; whichever runs second rebases.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>144, 145</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>12-18 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner round 2 item 6 (session 27): "Part 2 is extended across EVERY 'what's missing' item (all writers, ...)". Owner C10 answer: "documents, communications, memos, events and to-dos must be secure with the same contact access as the main record, via a server-side function" (CRITICAL). GitHub #1034 (word-add-in-r1 ISS-007) proposes the census.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make every server-side writer of a child record decide its owner through the ONE record-first owner resolver, so a child of a secure project, matter or work assignment is owned by the named Secure owner team and every other child by its parent's business-unit default team — and refuse the write when no owner can be resolved. Then add an architecture test that fails any future app-only create of a user-facing record that sets no owner.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer on the Dataverse write path (ADR-002 WP-1..WP-6) and the secure-isolation boundary. Expert in Dataverse ownership, the BFF's app-only writers and each writer's existing error contract. Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>Every BFF create or reparent of a child record listed in the census (step 1) sets `ownerid` from `IRecordOwnershipResolver` using the correct parent as the target; a child whose parent is secure (any of its parent lookups points at a secure root) is owned by task 144's named Secure owner team; a writer that cannot resolve an owner writes nothing and returns its own error contract with a message; an ArchTest census fails any new unowned app-only create of a user-facing record; contact access to children is unchanged; #1034 is closed with the outcome (coordinated with word-add-in-r1).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>WHY. C10 half 2 (session26 note): only the secure ROOT row is re-owned (`ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:609-616`); every child — document, communication, memo, event, to-do, analysis, invoice and the other tables `design.md` §5.1d enumerates (`design.md:552-603`, 18 entities / 19 lookups on sprk_project alone) — stays owned by its creator or by the BFF application user, in an ordinary business unit (usually ROOT). So a user with ordinary Deep/Local Read on those tables reads the children of a secure record in MDA with no share. DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md:124 records it as invariant I-2, "Not implemented … fail OPEN … Unowned".

THE ENGINE ALREADY EXISTS. `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs` (word-add-in-r1 task 080, invariant I-6): record-first — the target record's business unit, else the acting user's (`:144-214`); refuses when a NAMED target cannot be resolved (`:151-180`); registered at `Services/Dataverse/Extensions/MetadataServiceExtensions.cs:101-103`. On THIS branch `ResolveOwningTeamAsync` has ZERO callers (grep 2026-09-30: only its declaration `:66` and implementation `:144`). PR #1045 (OPEN) wires it for the Office writers only and changes the file (TOP 2 + ambiguity refusal, fault propagation, `DocumentAssociationMap.ToLogicalName` aliases, reads through `IGenericEntityService` — peer note 080 §6.3). Task 144 step 5 adds the secure branch: a target owned in the Secure Record BU resolves to the NAMED team, never the default team.

WHAT IS STILL MISSING AFTER 144 — this task's scope:
(1) THE WRITERS. #1034 lists ~20 app-only writers that set no owner. Verified anchors (2026-09-30, this branch):
  • External portal (CIAM/workforce contacts, app-only): `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs` `CreateDocumentAsync` :239 (binds `sprk_Project@odata.bind` :254), `CreateEventAsync` :579 (project-only bind :596), `CreateTodoAsync` :649 (POST :683); routes `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs` :125, :154, :169, :180, :210.
  • Communication: `Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs` sprk_communication :836, :1723, :1852; sprk_document :473, :2155, :2335; `IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs` sprk_communication :639 (created via `CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync` :690 → `Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs` :2948), sprk_document :932, :1114; `EmailUploadCaptureService.cs` :215 (create :87); `Channels/MessagingIngestor.cs` :199 (create :232); `MessageAttachmentMaterializer.cs` sprk_document :251 (create :259) — added by review 2026-09-30, absent from the #1034 list; `ThreadResolver.cs` sprk_communicationthread :138, :441, :568; `Access/DirectThreadAccessService.cs` :90 and `Threads/MessagingThreadKeyStrategy.cs` :71 (thread / channel-ref rows — classify).
  • Content-bearing rows hanging off a communication or analysis (added by review 2026-09-30 — the census MUST classify each; a row that carries a secure record's content or participants is a child and is fixed, not waived): `CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs` sprk_emailreviewlog creates (:1165, :1431, :1487, :1611, :1899, :1955), `CommunicationProposalApplyService.cs` / `CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService.cs` review-log creates (:710, :749, :812 / :790, :832), `CommunicationParticipantIndexer.cs` :104 (participant index rows), `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs` `CreateAnalysisOutputAsync` :598 (sprk_analysisoutput — AI output about a secure document), `CreateEmailArtifactAsync` :1940 / `CreateAttachmentArtifactAsync` :2022.
  • Inbound email documents: `Services/Email/EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs` :275 (`CreateDocumentAsync` — the resolver's own remarks name it as a no-acting-user writer; verify after the PR #1045 merge whether it is wired, and wire it here if not).
  • Events: `Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs` `CreateEventInDataverseAsync` :721-741 → `Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs` `CreateEventAsync` :409; `Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs` create :158.
  • To-dos: `Services/Workspace/TodoGenerationService.cs` :851 (owner parameter no caller passes — peer note 080 §6.5 item 3).
  • Analysis (×6+): `Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs` :187, :1207, :1405; `Services/Ai/AnalysisResultPersistence.cs` :126; `Services/Ai/AppOnlyAnalysisService.cs` :297, :1367; `Services/Insights/Observations/DataverseObservationMirror.cs` :174; all but the mirror go through `IAnalysisDataverseService.CreateAnalysisAsync` → `Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs` :430 (entity :440, create :466).
  • Finance/invoice: `Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs` :294-296 (create-by-upsert via `UpdateRecordFieldsAsync`), `SignalEvaluationService.cs` :226 (sprk_spendsignal), `SpendSnapshotService.cs` (sprk_spendsnapshot, :86).
  • Compose: `Services/Compose/ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.cs` :349 (`UpsertAsync`).
  • Run-as-user creates (owner defaults to the USER, in the user's BU — equally not isolated): `Services/Ai/Handlers/EmailDraftToolHandler.cs` :352, `Services/Ai/Handlers/DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs` :245.
  • Already wired by PR #1045 (verify after merge, do not redo): `OfficeService` save / to-do (:2766) / invoice (:2982), `UploadFinalizationWorker`, `POST /api/v1/documents`, `RecordCreationService`.
(2) REPARENT WRITES. A child moved UNDER a secure parent after creation must become secure too, and one moved out must stop being so. Server reparent writers include `IncomingAssociationResolver.ApplyDecisionAsync` (UpdateAsync, phase3-server-writers.md §2 row 4 — it only ADDS regarding fields, never clears) and the `CommunicationService.MapAssociationFields` call sites (row 2). A reparent that changes which parent is secure re-derives the owner.
(3) THE RIGHT TARGET. Children carry no `sprk_issecure`; securability comes from the parent. `sprk_document` has TWO project lookups (`sprk_project` and `sprk_relatedproject`, design.md:572) plus `sprk_matter` and `sprk_workassignment`, and carries NONE of the `sprk_regarding{core}` stamp columns (phase3-backfill-runbook.md §1b). `sprk_invoice` links by `sprk_matter`/`sprk_project`. Other children link by `sprk_regarding*` and carry the FR-26 core-ancestor stamp (`CoreAncestorResolver.cs:94-100`). The resolver takes ONE target today (`RecordOwnershipContext` :93-117). A writer that passes only its first lookup would miss a secure parent named in another.
(4) FLAGGED-BUT-NOT-ISOLATED PARENTS. Record-first derives the owner from the parent's OWNERSHIP. A root with `sprk_issecure = true` that is not (yet) owned by the named team — a failed or interrupted provisioning (C11, task 133) — would hand its children an ordinary BU. After task 150 locks the flag behind the endpoint this is only a failed-provision state, but it must fail closed.

CONTACT ACCESS IS UNAFFECTED BY OWNERSHIP. Contacts reach children through app-only reads keyed on the parent (session27 note, C10 research). This task must not change what a contact can see; task 056 (amended) extends contact coverage.</background>
