  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002 WP-1">Scope: all enforcement in this task. No Dataverse plugin. ONE server owner for the owner invariant: `IRecordOwnershipResolver`. No writer computes a team itself, and no second resolver, helper class or per-module team lookup is added (CLAUDE.md §11). Extend `RecordOwnershipContext`/`ResolveOwningTeamAsync` in place.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner C10 / session 27">Scope: parent derivation. Children carry no `sprk_issecure`; securability is derived from the parent. A child is secure if ANY of its parent lookups (every project/matter/work-assignment lookup the child table has, including BOTH `sprk_project` and `sprk_relatedproject` on `sprk_document`, and the FR-26 `sprk_regarding{core}` stamps where the table has them) points at a secure root. The writer passes ALL of those values; the resolver applies the rule. Lookup sets come from live metadata (the `CoreAncestorResolver.EntityColumnProbe` / MetadataService seam), never a hard-coded guess.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every writer changed. An unresolved owner, an unreadable parent, an ambiguous answer, or a parent with `sprk_issecure = true` that is NOT owned by task 144's named team REFUSES the write — nothing is created. It never falls back to app-user ownership, the caller's BU, or the Secure BU's default team. Each writer refuses in ITS OWN existing error contract (phase3-server-writers.md §4.3 table), with a message that names the reason; an HTTP surface returns a ProblemDetails with a stable reason code, never a bare 500. A Dataverse FAULT during resolution propagates as the caller's 5xx (peer F2), distinct from a refusal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: unfiled records. A document-only save with no related record is a REQUIRED use case: with no parent named, the resolver's acting-user fallback (§6.5 Path A already recorded by the peer) applies. Nothing in this task may make a target record required.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: background writers with no acting user (TodoGenerationService, IncomingCommunicationProcessor, MessagingIngestor, Finance jobs). A named parent always drives the owner; with no parent and no acting user the row is NOT created (logged with the reason, counted) — never app-owned. Best-effort writers keep their best-effort shape (a refusal is a skipped row, never a failed profile or a failed job — peer note 080 §6.6 for AppOnlyAnalysisService).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: per-user artifacts. Rows that are per-user by design — `appnotification`, `sprk_notificationoutbox`, `sprk_workspacelayout`, the per-user MASTER `sprk_communicationthread` — stay user-owned (peer note 080 §6.5 category C). Record threads REGARDING a secure parent are a decision point: see escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: contact access. Nothing in this task changes what a contact (CIAM or workforce) can read or write; the existing external suites stay green unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: SHIP-TOGETHER with task 149. Once a child is owned by the memberless secure team, internal users shared on the parent lose sight of it unless task 149's mechanism is live. This task's code may merge first behind no flag only if 149 merges in the same release; it MUST NOT be deployed to spaarke-bff-dev (or any shared environment) before 149 is merged. Record the pairing in the PR description.</constraint>
    <constraint source="coordination">Scope: word-add-in-r1. Do not re-implement anything PR #1045 ships (Office writers, the documents endpoint, the resolver hardening). #1034 is the peer's issue: message the word-add-in-r1 session before starting, take the census from them if they started one, and close #1034 once, citing both projects. sprk_communication is peer-handed-off to the Communication project (note 080 §6.6) — owner round 2 put ALL writers in scope here, so this task does it and tells that project.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no ctor null-check tests. Writer tests live under `tests/integration/data-mutation/**` (every new write path gets ≥1 integration test); resolver tests under `tests/unit/domain/Dataverse/`; the census under `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/`. Each fail-closed branch has a negative test; each guard is proven to bite by seeding.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` (no new service expected). Measure publish size against a FRESH master build from a short path with the same zip tool (Compress-Archive), report both sizes, the delta and file counts; ceiling 60 MB; run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: this task's deliverable. 100% of the server writers found by the census are fixed here; any writer discovered during execution is added to this task, not deferred. Do not relax the alternate key on the SPE item id (Compose/communication upserts).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2 item 11 / task 145 (added by review 2026-09-30)">Scope: the Secure Record Owner role's privileges. Dataverse refuses to assign a row to a team whose role lacks Read on that table. Every child table this task's census classifies "fix" MUST be in the ONE codified set (word-add-in-r1 task 082's JSON file, extended through task 145's procedure — never a second list) and granted live before this task's writers ship. A table the census finds that is not yet in the set is added in THIS task through 145's script and recorded in 145's note — not deferred and not left to a later run of 145.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner item 9 / task 152 (added by review 2026-09-30)">Scope: deployment ordering. Re-owning children that are user-owned today to a TEAM removes them from every surface that filters `owninguser = caller` — notably the Daily Briefing to-do channel (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Narrators/DailyBriefingCollector.cs:1027`, session27 note "Notifications research"). Run-as-user to-do/event writers (EmailDraftToolHandler, DataverseCreateRecordHandler) and the external-portal to-do create are affected. Task 152 (Assigned To / human Created By targeting) MUST be deployed to a shared environment no later than this task, or the owner must accept the interim drop-out (escalation). Record the ordering in the PR description.</constraint>
  </constraints>

