    <protocol>Load all files in knowledge before starting. Coordinate with word-add-in-r1 before the first edit to RecordOwnershipResolver.cs.</protocol>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-146" base="2a9b4b26c21e9aa6c95b245062cf19b4332e7137">
      <summary>Code complete, NOT deployed (ship-together with 149; deploy gates G146-1..3 first). Every BFF create and re-file of a child / content row now decides ownerid through IRecordOwnershipResolver (extended in place): secure-if-any over EVERY parent lookup the row carries (sprk_document's six root lookups included), a root flagged sprk_issecure but not owned in the Secure BU REFUSES, a re-file applies the change then assigns the owner in a separate write and reads it back, a Dataverse fault propagates (never a refusal). Each writer refuses in its own contract (HTTP 409 ProblemDetails + stable reasonCode via ProblemDetailsHelper.RecordOwnerRefused; background/best-effort log-and-skip; AI task core degraded Guid.Empty; inbound email HELD per amendment R3). Full census with file:line, dispositions and live parent-lookup sets: notes/task-146-server-child-writers.md.</summary>
      <files>RecordOwnershipResolver.cs (context Parents/ForChild/ForParents/ContentOf, KeepCreator, RecordOwnerResolution + ApplyTo, ReparentAsync, IsReparentableChild, RecordOwnerUnresolvedException); writers: ExternalDataService + ExternalProjectDataEndpoints, CommunicationService, IncomingCommunicationProcessor, IncomingAssociationResolver, EmailUploadCaptureService, ThreadResolver, CommunicationParticipantIndexer, CommunicationEnrichmentService, CommunicationProposalApplyService, CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService, MessageAttachmentMaterializer, EmailAttachmentProcessor, EventEndpoints (+ event logs), DataverseWebApiService, DataverseServiceClientImpl (seams), TaskActionCore / CreateTaskNodeExecutor / ActionSeam, UpdateRecordActionCore, DataverseUpdateHandler, TodoGenerationService, AnalysisEndpoints, AnalysisResultPersistence, AppOnlyAnalysisService, ReviewMemoEndpoints, DataverseObservationMirror, SignalEvaluationService, SpendSnapshotService, InvoiceReviewService (document link = reparent), Compose promoter/service/endpoint, DataverseDocumentsEndpoints (PUT re-file), RecordMatchEndpoints, DocumentCheckoutService (+ DocumentOperationsEndpoints 409), UploadFinalizationWorker artifacts, OfficeService to-do (secure-if-any), IncomingCommunicationJobHandler (hold), CommunicationOptions.OwnershipHoldAlertUserIds, ProblemDetailsHelper.RecordOwnerRefused; docs DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md rows I-2, I-6; config/secure-record-owner-role.json (+17 child tables, evidence pending); tests (below).</files>
      <tests>New: tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (7); tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/SecureChildOwnershipTests.cs (17, REAL resolver over the shared OwnershipDirectory); RecordOwnershipResolverTests (35). Seed-and-bite: 4 census guards + 3 writer families each failed when seeded and passed after restore (files touched). Existing suites updated only where the contract changed (task owner = team, record thread owner = team, JOIN reads the thread row, hosts register RecordOwnershipResolverDouble, invoice confirm = reparent); 3 ADR-038-banned ctor null-check tests deleted. External-access expectations unchanged. Counts: see the task's final report.</tests>
      <placement>No new service, endpoint, package, DI registration or job (bff-extensions.md: extend-in-place; the writers became callers of the existing singleton resolver). ONE new option key, CommunicationOptions.OwnershipHoldAlertUserIds (§11: existing = none, grep found only DemoProvisioningOptions.AdminNotificationEmails for registration email; extension = the existing Communication section, not a new one; cost-of-doing-nothing = amendment R3's administrator alert has no recipient, so a held email would only be visible in logs). Shared test harness OwnershipDirectory moved out of RecordOwnershipResolverTests (no new logic). Publish size: measured by the main session (task brief).</placement>
